nc-fixer-insider-name = John "Insider" Doe
nc-fixer-insider-desc = One anonymous journalist, or several. Runs an underground outlet that exposes corps and city hall with open sources, leaks and a private network of insiders; lately also the dirty secrets of medtech and research giants. Never shows a face: works through the Net, rarely through go-betweens. Always hungry for new material and pays well for names, blueprints and facts.
nc-fixer-insider-greeting-1 = > CONNECTION ENCRYPTED. "Got something for me? Names, schematics, anything that makes them sweat."
nc-fixer-insider-greeting-2 = > RELAY 7 OF 12. "The public deserves to know. And you deserve to get paid."
nc-fixer-insider-greeting-3 = > SIGNAL SCRAMBLED. "Don't look for me. Look for the truth, then send it my way."
nc-fixer-vlad-name = Vladimir "Vlad" Grigoriev
nc-fixer-vlad-desc = An emigrant and former member of an Eastern European crime ring, rumoured to have been convicted back home for trafficking. Fled to Night City and dug in at a dock in the port. Before the Time of the Red he built a network of buyers and runners supplying wholesale clients with guns and drugs. The Fourth Corporate War cost him his sea routes and his smuggler's clout, so now he lives off old stock: dope, fencing and storing stolen goods, finding and moving supplies around the city.
nc-fixer-vlad-greeting-1 = "Privet, choom. Work is there, money is there. Questions — not there."
nc-fixer-vlad-greeting-2 = "Port is quiet today. Quiet is good for business. You want business?"
nc-fixer-vlad-greeting-3 = "Vlad remembers who pays and who does not. Better you are the first kind."

nc-fixer-mission-insider-leak = The leak
nc-fixer-mission-insider-leak-desc = A source of mine left a shard at a quiet spot and went dark. Pick it up and put it in my drop.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-tyger-names = Who pays the Claws
nc-fixer-mission-insider-tyger-names-desc = The Tyger Claws keep a list of everyone paying them for protection on a terminal. Crack it and bring me the names.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-maelstrom-names = Maelstrom's buyers
nc-fixer-mission-insider-maelstrom-names-desc = Somebody respectable buys chrome from Maelstrom. Their terminal knows who. So will I.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-arrests = Arrest records
nc-fixer-mission-insider-arrests-desc = NCPD buries arrests that embarrass the right people. Get into a precinct terminal and pull the records.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-militech-ops = Militech operations
nc-fixer-mission-insider-militech-ops-desc = Militech is planning something off the books. Crack a terminal at one of their sites and copy the operation files.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-biotech-trials = Clinical trials
nc-fixer-mission-insider-biotech-trials-desc = Biotechnica tests drugs on people who never signed anything. The trial data sits on a terminal at their site.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-biotech-lab = The lab's dirty secret
nc-fixer-mission-insider-biotech-lab-desc = A Biotechnica lab hides research that would end careers. Security is heavy. The story is worth it.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-medtech-boosters = Chrome for boosters
nc-fixer-mission-insider-medtech-boosters-desc = Medical Technologies grows replacement limbs in the port and sells cyberware to boostergangs on the side. The customer list sits on a terminal in their building. Three floors, armed staff with pistols and blades. Bring me the shard.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-corporate-pda = Someone's PDA
nc-fixer-mission-insider-corporate-pda-desc = A corp employee carries their whole work life in a PDA. Bring it to my drop and I'll take it from there.

nc-fixer-mission-vlad-push = Push the product
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-push-desc = Take the brick. Buyer waits at drop point. You leave it, you go. Simple.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-push-maelstrom = Delivery for Maelstrom
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-push-maelstrom-desc = Maelstrom wants product. They pay well, they shoot fast. Leave the brick at the drop and do not make them nervous.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-guns = Iron for a client
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-guns-desc = Client needs four Streetmasters. Where you find — not my problem. Put them in my drop.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-ammo = Ammunition
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-ammo-desc = Six magazines of nine millimetre. Full ones. Into my drop.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-dope = Party supplies
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-dope-desc = Ten doses of euphoric. Street quality is fine, my clients are not picky.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-meds = Medicine for resale
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-meds-desc = Ten doses of trauma painkiller. Hospitals have, Vlad needs. Into my drop.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-debtor = Debt collection
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-debtor-desc = This man owes Vlad. Find him, beat him well. Alive. Dead men do not pay.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-debtor-valentinos = Debtor under protection
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-debtor-valentinos-desc = My debtor runs to Valentinos and thinks he is safe. Show him he is wrong. Alive, and do not start a war.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-medtech-vats = Spoiled harvest
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-medtech-vats-desc = Medical Technologies grows arms and legs in the port and sells chrome to boosters on my streets. Vlad does not like competition. Break the machine that runs their vats. Their doctors carry guns and machetes, be ready.

ent-NCFixerInsider = net terminal
    .desc = A public Net access point. The screen shows a masked face and a blinking cursor.
ent-NCFixerVlad = Vladimir Grigoriev
    .desc = A heavyset man in a leather jacket and a striped undershirt, cigarette in his teeth.
ent-NCFixerDeadDropBase = dead drop
    .desc = A fixer's dead drop. Goods go in, money comes out.
ent-NCMissionMarkerBase = mission marker
    .desc = Mapping marker for fixer missions.
ent-NCMissionPackage = sealed package
    .desc = Taped shut. Better not ask.
ent-NCMissionDataShard = data shard
    .desc = An encrypted data shard.
ent-NCMissionSabotageTarget = server rack
    .desc = Humming hardware. Somebody wants it gone.

nc-mission-guard-warning-1 = Hey. Private business here. Walk away.
nc-mission-guard-warning-2 = You lost? Keep moving, choom.
nc-mission-guard-alarm-1 = That's it, light 'em up!
nc-mission-guard-alarm-2 = Intruder! Take them down!

ent-NCMissionDrugBrick = taped brick
    .desc = Something pressed and wrapped in tape. Vlad's product.
ent-NCMissionIntelTerminal = data terminal
    .desc = A locked terminal. Someone wants what is on it.
ent-NCMobHumanDebtor = debtor
    .desc = Owes money to the wrong people.

nc-fixer-kind-recon = Recon
nc-fixer-kind-laundering = Laundering
nc-fixer-mission-hostile = Things turned violent and the deal is off: {$mission} failed.
nc-fixer-recon-progress = Point scouted: {$done} of {$total}.
nc-fixer-map-recon = Scout
nc-fixer-launder-target = wire {$amount} €$ to {$account}
nc-fixer-launder-credited = {$amount} €$ just landed on your account from nowhere. Wire all of it to {$account} before time runs out. That transfer carries no fee.
nc-fixer-launder-progress = Wired so far: {$done} of {$total} €$.
nc-fixer-launder-taken = The fixer's people took {$amount} €$ back from your account.
nc-mission-owner-hot-zone = Hot Zone
nc-mission-owner-scavengers = Scavengers

nc-fixer-tabitha-name = Tabitha "Jay" Jones
nc-fixer-tabitha-desc = A former nomad who left her clan and moved to the city. With her family's wisdom she brokers between enemies and allies, settling gangs and striking deals, which earned her a fine name among Solos. Through old friends she knows how to find and bring in rare, one-of-a-kind goods from all over North America and the NUSA. Rumour says she runs a shop that modifies guns and files off serial numbers.
nc-fixer-tabitha-greeting-1 = "Sit down, choom. Everybody wants something. Let's see what you want."
nc-fixer-tabitha-greeting-2 = "My clan taught me one thing: nobody wins a war. Some just lose slower."
nc-fixer-tabitha-greeting-3 = "Rare iron, rare names, rare deals. Which one are you here for?"
nc-fixer-feng-name = Josie Feng
nc-fixer-feng-desc = A woman of the Chinese diaspora. Before the Time of the Red she owned a chain of restaurants and shops; afterwards she turned to night clubs and bars, growing the entertainment trade in her districts and drawing rich clients who want a thrill. She also runs the night markets: through her connections private buyers get what they want and ordinary operators can sell their goods and services.
nc-fixer-feng-greeting-1 = "The night is young and so are my clients. Let's make them happy."
nc-fixer-feng-greeting-2 = "Everything has a price at my market. Even you."
nc-fixer-feng-greeting-3 = "My clubs run smooth because people like you keep them smooth."
nc-fixer-vance-name = Declan Vance
nc-fixer-vance-desc = A freelance auditor and, before the Time of the Red, a union leader. He takes no corporate contracts but often advises their people on delicate questions such as takeovers. Staying neutral with everyone, he helps private persons and businesses distribute goods and services, and corporations with the local market. The street says Vance hides gangs' illegal work behind legal fronts: he adjusts the figures, the tax returns and the shop window of a "clean" business.
nc-fixer-vance-greeting-1 = "Numbers never lie. People make them say what they need."
nc-fixer-vance-greeting-2 = "I'm neutral, friend. Neutrality is expensive, so let's talk business."
nc-fixer-vance-greeting-3 = "Quietly, please. Clean books need a quiet room."
nc-fixer-botha-name = Pieter Botha
nc-fixer-botha-desc = A soldier from South Africa who claims to have fought in the Fourth Corporate War and served in a corporation's security in Night City. Finding no place after the Time of the Red, he chose to live in the past, going back into the Hot Zone again and again for tech, documents and other valuables in the ruins. Later he found like minds and began leading expeditions and raids himself.
nc-fixer-botha-greeting-1 = "The Zone remembers the war better than anyone. Ready to dig?"
nc-fixer-botha-greeting-2 = "Rule one in the ruins: the Scavengers saw you first."
nc-fixer-botha-greeting-3 = "There's still a fortune under the rubble. Bring it back and we split."

nc-fixer-mission-tabithaleaderstygerclaws = Who runs the Claws
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaleaderstygerclaws-desc = Before I sit the Tyger Claws down at a table, I need to know who really calls the shots. Crack their terminal and bring the names.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaleadersvalentinos = Who runs the Valentinos
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaleadersvalentinos-desc = The Valentinos say "familia", but somebody is the head of it. Get the names off their terminal.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaleadersmaelstrom = Who runs Maelstrom
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaleadersmaelstrom-desc = Maelstrom changes bosses like chrome. I need the current ones. Their terminal knows.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaturfbozos = Bozos turf
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaturfbozos-desc = Walk the Bozos' ground and see what they really hold. Three points, eyes open, don't start the circus.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaturfinquisitors = Inquisitors turf
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaturfinquisitors-desc = The Inquisitors claim more blocks than they can pray over. Check three of their points.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaturfphilharmonicvampyres = Vampyres turf
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaturfphilharmonicvampyres-desc = Find out where the Philharmonic Vampyres really play. Three points, and no screaming.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithatrucevalentinos = A gift for the Valentinos
nc-fixer-mission-tabithatrucevalentinos-desc = Take my gift to the Valentinos and leave it at the drop. If anyone draws a gun, the truce is dead and so is the job.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithatrucetygerclaws = A gift for the Claws
nc-fixer-mission-tabithatrucetygerclaws-desc = The Claws want respect before they talk. Bring them my gift, bow if you must, but no fighting.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithagunmallorian = A Mallorian for a client
nc-fixer-mission-tabithagunmallorian-desc = A client wants a Mallorian Arms 12 mm. Find one and leave it in my drop.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithagunburya = A Burya for a client
nc-fixer-mission-tabithagunburya-desc = Somebody wants a Burya revolver. Rare iron. Find it.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaguncopperhead = A Copperhead
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaguncopperhead-desc = A Copperhead rifle, no questions asked. Into my drop.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithagunnomad = A nomad long gun
nc-fixer-mission-tabithagunnomad-desc = My people want their sniper rifle back home. Find one like it.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaammomallorian = Mallorian magazines
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaammomallorian-desc = Three Mallorian 12 mm magazines. Make them or find them.
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaammoburya = Burya rounds
nc-fixer-mission-tabithaammoburya-desc = Two boxes of 14 mm Burya rounds. Hard to find, easy to print if you know where.

nc-fixer-mission-fengparty = Party delivery
nc-fixer-mission-fengparty-desc = A crate for tonight's party. Take it to the club's drop and don't open it.
nc-fixer-mission-fengvipclient = A VIP's order
nc-fixer-mission-fengvipclient-desc = A rich guest wants two bottles of whiskey, two of wine and a box of cigars. Put them in my drop.
nc-fixer-mission-fengtroublemaker = Trouble at the club
nc-fixer-mission-fengtroublemaker-desc = A guest is making a scene. Calm him down. Firmly. Alive.
nc-fixer-mission-fengnightmarket = Night market cut
nc-fixer-mission-fengnightmarket-desc = My cut from the night market is waiting in an envelope. Pick it up and bring it to my drop.
nc-fixer-mission-fengnightmarketclaws = Cut from the Claws
nc-fixer-mission-fengnightmarketclaws-desc = The Tyger Claws hold my envelope and forget whose market it is. Remind them.
nc-fixer-mission-fengcompetitor = Kill the music
nc-fixer-mission-fengcompetitor-desc = A rival club steals my guests. Wreck their sound system.

nc-fixer-mission-vancesnitch = A loose mouth
nc-fixer-mission-vancesnitch-desc = Someone is talking to the wrong people about my clients' books. Make sure he talks to no one.
nc-fixer-mission-vancelaundersmall = Small change
nc-fixer-mission-vancelaundersmall-desc = Money lands on your account; you wire it on to my company. You keep ten percent for the trouble.
nc-fixer-mission-vancelaundermedium = A clean transfer
nc-fixer-mission-vancelaundermedium-desc = A bigger sum this time. Same rules: receive, wire it on, keep your ten percent.
nc-fixer-mission-vancelaunderlarge = Big money
nc-fixer-mission-vancelaunderlarge-desc = Ten thousand that never existed. Wire it on in time and nobody will ever ask.
nc-fixer-mission-vancearson = A business accident
nc-fixer-mission-vancearson-desc = A competitor keeps their books in a cabinet at their office. Burn the books. Fire is the cleanest auditor.
nc-fixer-mission-vancebankhack = Account access
nc-fixer-mission-vancebankhack-desc = A terminal at a business office holds the keys to an account I'm interested in. Crack it and bring me the shard.

nc-fixer-mission-bothatechcrate = Pre-war tech
nc-fixer-mission-bothatechcrate-desc = We marked a crate of pre-war tech in the ruins. The Scavengers marked it too. Bring it out.
nc-fixer-mission-bothadocuments = Corporate files
nc-fixer-mission-bothadocuments-desc = A dead corporation's files survived in a collapsed office. They are worth more than the building was.
nc-fixer-mission-bothaprototype = Military prototype
nc-fixer-mission-bothaprototype-desc = A military prototype from the war is lying in a Scavengers' nest. Heavy guard. Heavy pay.
nc-fixer-mission-bothaoldnet = The old Net
nc-fixer-mission-bothaoldnet-desc = A terminal of the old Net still has power in the ruins. Crack it and bring what's left.
nc-fixer-mission-bothaoldnetdeep = Deep in the old Net
nc-fixer-mission-bothaoldnetdeep-desc = The best data sits where the Scavengers sleep. Crack the old terminal in their camp.

ent-NCFixerTabitha = Tabitha Jones
    .desc = A woman in a road-worn nomad jacket, watching everyone at once.
ent-NCFixerFeng = Josie Feng
    .desc = An elegant woman in red silk with an earpiece and a cold smile.
ent-NCFixerVance = Declan Vance
    .desc = A grey-suited man with glasses and a briefcase that never leaves his hand.
ent-NCFixerBotha = Pieter Botha
    .desc = A weathered veteran in old fatigues and a beret, a rifle slung on his back.
ent-NCMissionPeaceOffering = gift box
    .desc = A lacquered box with a ribbon. A peace offering.
ent-NCMissionPartyCrate = party crate
    .desc = Clinking and rattling. Better not to ask what for.
ent-NCMissionCashEnvelope = thick envelope
    .desc = Stuffed with eddies and sealed with wax.
ent-NCMissionHotZoneTechCrate = pre-war tech crate
    .desc = A battered crate full of pre-war electronics.
ent-NCMissionMilitaryPrototype = military prototype
    .desc = An unfinished weapon system from the Fourth Corporate War.
ent-NCMissionCorporateFiles = corporate files
    .desc = A folder of a dead corporation's documents. Still dangerous.
ent-NCMissionOldNetTerminal = old Net terminal
    .desc = A pre-war terminal still humming in the ruins.
ent-NCMissionClubSoundSystem = club sound system
    .desc = Towers of speakers and a mixing desk.
ent-NCMissionLedgerCabinet = ledger cabinet
    .desc = A cabinet full of paper ledgers. Very flammable.

nc-fixer-mission-vance-manifests = Doctored manifests
nc-fixer-mission-vance-manifests-desc = Containers vanish between the ship and the customs shed, and the paperwork says they never existed. 6th Street keeps the real manifests on a terminal in the basement of W 22nd Street 02, South Night City. Copy them for me.
nc-fixer-mission-botha-lost-container = Lost container
nc-fixer-mission-botha-lost-container-desc = A military prototype fell off a ship in the port, straight into a 6th Street warehouse under W 22nd Street 02. Their soldiers guard it like family silver. Bring it to me.
nc-fixer-mission-feng-bad-chrome = Bad chrome
nc-fixer-mission-feng-bad-chrome-desc = A Maelstrom ripperdoc in a South Night City back alley fits cheap chrome to my clubs' regulars, and they come back to me in body bags. Close his practice. Permanently.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-push-sixth-street = Goods for 6th Street
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-push-sixth-street-desc = 6th Street buys from Vlad and sells at the port. Take the brick to their drop in South Night City. Their boys will be waiting, do not make them nervous.

cmd-ncrep-desc = Shows or sets the street reputation of a player's current character.
cmd-ncrep-help = Usage: {$command} <username> [value]
cmd-ncrep-arg-user = <username>
cmd-ncrep-arg-value = [value 0-{$max}]
cmd-ncrep-error-args = Expected a username and an optional value.
cmd-ncrep-error-no-character = {$username} is not playing a character right now.
cmd-ncrep-error-value = The value must be a whole number from 0 to {$max}.
cmd-ncrep-result = {$username}: street reputation {$value} ({$level}).

nc-fixer-mission-insider-ncu-research = Open access
nc-fixer-mission-insider-ncu-research-desc = Night City University's cyberware lab is sitting on research three corps would kill for. The data never leaves their own terminals. Get into the lab or the server vault, pull it onto a shard and walk it out. Campus security is armed and takes "protecting knowledge" literally.
nc-fixer-mission-vance-campus-recon = Campus tour
nc-fixer-mission-vance-campus-recon-desc = A client wants to know how Night City University guards its labs and its server vault. Walk the halls, stand where the good stuff is kept, and do not start anything.
nc-fixer-mission-feng-inquisitors-broadcast = Dead air
nc-fixer-mission-feng-inquisitors-broadcast-desc = The Inquisitors squat in the old lecture annex by the university and broadcast sermons against "chromed filth" every night. My club kids are getting jumped on the way home. Smash their broadcast rig.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-student-dealer = Tuition fees
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-student-dealer-desc = A student sells my goods around the university and keeps the money for himself. Find him and explain the business. Hands only, I want him able to pay.

nc-fixer-mission-vance-vampyres-blackmail = Velvet tapes
nc-fixer-mission-vance-vampyres-blackmail-desc = The Philharmonic Vampyres film everything that happens in the salon under their Downtown club, and half the district's executives have been down there. Get into the salon, pull the recordings off their terminal and bring me the shard.
nc-fixer-mission-feng-bad-blood = Bad blood
nc-fixer-mission-feng-bad-blood-desc = The Vampyres' host keeps poaching my best customers and sending them back drained and broken. He holds court under their club in Downtown. End the party.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-n54-footage = Hot material
nc-fixer-mission-insider-n54-footage-desc = Network 54 sat on footage someone paid them to bury. It is still on the bureau's servers on 14th Street. Get into the bureau, copy it onto a shard and get out before their security works out you are not a guest.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-room-service = Room service
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-room-service-desc = A guest of mine is waiting for a package. Take it, leave it where I tell you and walk away like you were never there.

nc-fixer-mission-feng-rigged-pachinko = Rigged drum
nc-fixer-mission-feng-rigged-pachinko-desc = The Tyger Claws' pachinko house in Old Japantown pays out only when they want it to, and my regulars lose their rent there every week. The machines run off one server in the back. Wreck it.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-maelstrom-neighbours = New neighbours
nc-fixer-mission-insider-maelstrom-neighbours-desc = Maelstrom opened a garage on the Tyger Claws' doorstep in Old Japantown. Somebody wants to know what they keep in there. Walk their ground, stand where it matters and leave before they notice.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-chrome-parcel = Parcel for the chrome
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-chrome-parcel-desc = Maelstrom pays well and pays on time, which is more than most. Take this to their garage drop. Do not stare at their faces.

nc-fixer-mission-vance-scavenger-nest = The nest
nc-fixer-mission-vance-scavenger-nest-desc = The Scavengers' boss sits in a sniper nest at the top of what is left of Arasaka Tower and shoots anyone crossing the old plaza. Climb the stump through the fallout and put him down.
nc-fixer-mission-tabitha-dead-zone-map = Map of the dead zone
nc-fixer-mission-tabitha-dead-zone-map-desc = Nobody has a current map of the Scavengers' ground at ground zero: the camps, the chop shop, the tunnels under the plaza. Walk them all and come back with it. Bring a rad suit.
nc-fixer-mission-feng-rusty-conveyor = Rusty conveyor
nc-fixer-mission-feng-rusty-conveyor-desc = The Scavengers strip anything that comes out of the hot zone on a conveyor line under their camp and sell it in my clubs as clean chrome. Break the line.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-debt-in-the-dark = Debt in the dark
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-debt-in-the-dark-desc = A man who owes me thinks the old metro under ground zero is a good place to hide. Go down there and remind him. Alive, he still owes.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-ash-server = Ash server
nc-fixer-mission-insider-ash-server-desc = Under the plaza there is an Arasaka data center that survived the blast, and an Old Net terminal still talks to it. Scavengers squat on top of it. Get to the terminal and pull what is on it.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-black-vault = The Black Vault
nc-fixer-mission-insider-black-vault-desc = Below the data center lies a vault Arasaka never admitted to building, and its sleepers are still on watch. Its core holds data from before the war. Get through the checkpoint, reach the core and copy it. Expect turrets.
nc-fixer-mission-botha-legacy = Legacy
nc-fixer-mission-botha-legacy-desc = Arasaka left prototypes in the Black Vault under ground zero, and a buyer wants one badly enough to pay this much. The vault's guards will not hand it over.
nc-fixer-mission-vance-sleeper = The sleeper
nc-fixer-mission-vance-sleeper-desc = The commander of the Black Vault has kept his post for twenty years and still sends his blades up after anyone who gets close. A client wants the post vacated. Permanently.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-cold-reactor = Cold reactor
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-cold-reactor-desc = The Black Vault runs on its own power. Kill the reactor controls and the whole vault goes dark for whoever comes next. The sleepers will not like it.

nc-fixer-not-employee = "Staff only. Your ID does not clear."
nc-fixer-mission-paid-employer = {$mission} done. {$reward} €$ credited to the field office and HQ accounts.
nc-fixer-militech-ops-name = Militech operations console
nc-fixer-militech-ops-desc = The field office's secure terminal. HQ posts operations here that the budget does not cover; every completed job funds the office and its parent division.
nc-fixer-militech-ops-greeting-1 = > MILITECH SECURE NET. Authentication accepted. Open operations:
nc-fixer-militech-ops-greeting-2 = > FIELD OFFICE NC-7. Budget shortfall noted. Operations available for funding.
nc-fixer-militech-ops-greeting-3 = > PRIORITY CHANNEL. Report completion through this terminal.
ent-NCFixerMilitechOps = Militech operations console
    .desc = The field office's secure console with the list of open operations.
ent-NCFixerDeadDropMilitechOps = Militech evidence locker
    .desc = Recovered items go in here for HQ.

nc-militech-contract-arasaka-prototype = Asset recovery: Arasaka prototype
nc-militech-contract-arasaka-prototype-desc = R&D wants an Arasaka prototype from the Black Vault under ground zero. Recover one and secure it in the evidence locker. Expect heavy resistance and turrets.
nc-militech-contract-vault-data = Intelligence: Black Vault core
nc-militech-contract-vault-data-desc = Copy the Black Vault's server core before anyone else does. Hack a core terminal, bring the shard to the evidence locker.
nc-militech-contract-vault-recon = Reconnaissance: Black Vault
nc-militech-contract-vault-recon-desc = HQ needs eyes on the Arasaka remnant's positions. Reach the marked points inside the vault and report. Engagement is at your discretion.
nc-militech-contract-stolen-crates = Asset recovery: stolen crates
nc-militech-contract-stolen-crates-desc = A shipment of Militech hardware went missing at the port and turned up in a 6th Street store. Recover a crate.
nc-militech-contract-maelstrom-broker = Neutralisation: Maelstrom broker
nc-militech-contract-maelstrom-broker-desc = A Maelstrom boss is selling stolen Militech cyberware on the street. Neutralise him.
nc-militech-contract-tyger-cache = Denial: Tyger Claws cache
nc-militech-contract-tyger-cache-desc = The Tyger Claws keep a hardware server in their Old Japantown house that routes Arasaka-pattern weapons. Destroy it.
nc-militech-contract-n-5-4-leak = Containment: Network 54 footage
nc-militech-contract-n-5-4-leak-desc = Network 54 holds footage of a Militech operation that must not air. Pull it from their bureau servers before it does.
nc-militech-contract-hot-zone-salvage = Asset recovery: hot zone salvage
nc-militech-contract-hot-zone-salvage-desc = Scavengers are stripping pre-war tech out of ground zero. Recover a tech crate before they sell it on.
nc-militech-contract-med-tech-line = Denial: Medical Technologies supply line
nc-militech-contract-med-tech-line-desc = Medical Technologies is arming boostergangs with cyberware grown in the port. Shut down their vat controller.
nc-fixer-console-offers-title = Open operations
nc-fixer-console-funds = Rewards go to the company: {$share}% to the field office, the rest to headquarters.
nc-fixer-console-offer-terms = {$reward} €$ to the company · {$minutes} min
nc-fixer-console-offer-locked = Staff only

nc-fixer-mission-vance-lights-out = Lights out
nc-fixer-mission-vance-lights-out-desc = The Scavengers run their tunnels under ground zero off a stolen power relay. Kill it and the whole warren goes dark for my client's crew.
nc-fixer-mission-feng-metro-butcher = Butcher of the metro
nc-fixer-mission-feng-metro-butcher-desc = A Scavenger boss down in the old metro strips people who wander too far, and two of my bartenders were among them. Find him in the tunnels and end it.
nc-fixer-mission-tabitha-metro-survey = Metro survey
nc-fixer-mission-tabitha-metro-survey-desc = A nomad crew wants a route through the tunnels under ground zero. Walk the platform, the tunnels and the workshop and mark where the Scavengers sit.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-down-the-line = Down the line
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-down-the-line-desc = The Scavengers in the tunnels buy from me too. Take this down to their drop. It is dark down there; walk slowly and keep your hands visible.
nc-fixer-mission-botha-metro-cache = Metro cache
nc-fixer-mission-botha-metro-cache-desc = The Scavengers stash the best hot zone salvage in the tunnels before they sell it. A buyer wants a crate before they do.
nc-fixer-mission-botha-vault-blueprints = Vault blueprints
nc-fixer-mission-botha-vault-blueprints-desc = Somewhere in the Black Vault is a folder of Arasaka blueprints that never made it to Tokyo. Bring it to me and you will never need another job this year.
nc-fixer-mission-insider-ghost-in-the-core = Ghost in the core
nc-fixer-mission-insider-ghost-in-the-core-desc = Nobody has ever walked the Black Vault and talked about it. Go in, stand where it matters, come out. The story is worth more than any shard.

nc-fixer-mission-vlad-valentinos-books = Burn the books
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-valentinos-books-desc = The Valentinos keep their debt book in a cabinet somewhere in the cantina. Half of 27th Street owes them, and some of those debts are mine. Wreck it.
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-valentinos-turf = Valentinos turf
nc-fixer-mission-vlad-valentinos-turf-desc = Someone wants to know how the Valentinos hold Ventura Street. Walk their cantina, their garage and their junkyard, then tell me who sits where.
nc-fixer-mission-feng-bozos-king = The clown king
nc-fixer-mission-feng-bozos-king-desc = The Bozos crowned a new king in the old Ventura cinema, and his first decree was to burn one of my bars. He has to go.
nc-fixer-mission-feng-bozos-party = Party favours
nc-fixer-mission-feng-bozos-party-desc = The Bozos are throwing a party and I am buying peace with a crate of the good stuff. Take it to their drop at the cinema and do not laugh at anyone.
nc-fixer-mission-botha-valentinos-cash = Garage money
nc-fixer-mission-botha-valentinos-cash-desc = The Valentinos count the chop-shop money before it goes to the bank. One envelope going missing on the way is a tragedy for them and a pay day for us.
nc-fixer-mission-botha-bozos-stash = Clown candy
nc-fixer-mission-botha-bozos-stash-desc = The Bozos sit on a brick of something nasty in their cinema. My buyer wants it off the street and in his hands.
